{
    "method": "autoresearch.autoresearchTrainCreate",
    "toolName": "autoresearch-train-create",
    "operationId": "autoresearch_train_create",
    "title": "Start training",
    "category": "Autoresearch",
    "description": "Start an asynchronous training run for a pipeline. Launches the autoresearch agent in a sandbox and returns the training run immediately with status 'running'. Poll autoresearch-training-runs-list until the run reaches 'completed' or 'failed'. A pipeline's first run has no champion until it completes and server-side promotion runs; on a retrain the existing champion keeps scoring until a new one is promoted. Returns 400 if a training run is already in progress, the pipeline is paused, or its creator or target is no longer valid (recreate the pipeline). Returns 403 from inside a sandbox, such as a PostHog AI cloud task: do not retry, and ask the user to start training from the pipeline's page in PostHog. Needs PostHog Desktop access, because the run is a cloud sandbox. After a run promotes a champion, the daily 02:00 UTC scoring job scores the inference population and emits autoresearch_prediction events. To score now instead, call autoresearch-score-create once. You can optionally override the iteration_budget for this run. A pipeline with an action target also needs the action:read scope.",
    "requiredScopes": ["autoresearch:write", "query:read", "insight:read"],
    "annotations": {
        "readOnly": false,
        "destructive": false,
        "idempotent": false
    },
    "availability": ["feature_flag: autoresearch"],
    "methodSource": "src/generated/autoresearch/client.ts",
